==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[longshot]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[long]] [[shot]]}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic|nautical}} Something [[unlikely]]; something that has little [[chance]] of happening or working. The term arose from the accuracy of early ship guns, which were effective only at close range and unlikely to hit the mark at any great distance.
#: ''We can try your plan, but it's a '''long shot''' and it probably won't work.''
# {{label|en|film}} A [[master]] shot, the primary wide [[shot]] of a [[scene]] into which the [[closeup]]s will be edited later.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|film}} [[establishing shot]], [[wide shot]]

